  "description": "MUGYES crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H148 Er4 N8 O12. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 5 O neighbors; Er1K (Er) has 5 O neighbors; Er1G (Er) has 5 O neighbors; Er1N (Er) has 5 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 5 O neighbors; Er2K (Er) has 5 O neighbors; Er2G (Er) has 5 O neighbors; Er2N (Er) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.817-3.912 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.75-108.60°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H148N8O12Er4.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
